From: HardDinD developers
Subject: [EXPERIMENT] um: retain host mapping identity for protection and lazy fork

Default off: uml_fault_hostmap=1 coalesces permission-only changes with mprotect.
Applies directly after the default series; no profiling candidate is required.
uml_fault_lazy=1 defers old PTEs installed into empty slots of a fresh user mm,
before its first TLB synchronization. Later PFN replacements always use mmap.
Normal guest fork/COW, memory accounting, and synchronous invalidation remain.
Copied PTEs never inherit host ownership: set_pte derives it from its old slot.
No user runners or guest address spaces are shared across fork or exec.

